1 0 0 1 48 729 Tm (Appealing an HOA Fine in Court) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 716 Tm (Educational use only. Not legal advice. Verify against your CC&Rs and state law.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 703 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 48 690 Tm (== VISUAL SUMMARY ==) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 677 Tm (Five takeaways to remember about exhaustion, jurisdiction, and evidence preservation. Use) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 664 Tm (them as a one-page briefing before you write or speak.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 651 Tm (* Start with procedure: Map notice, cure, hearing, and decision duties before debating the aesthetics of exhaustion, jurisdiction, and evidence preservation.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 638 Tm (* Make the decision point explicit: Your appeal should answer whether court is proportionate to the dispute with exhibits, not adjectives.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 625 Tm (* Compare options deliberately: Know whether you are closer to Small claims, Civil court, or ADR first before you escalate.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 612 Tm (* Write one remedy sentence: Boards skim-state waive, reduce, re-notice, or reverse in a single line tied to exhaustion, jurisdiction, and evidence preservation.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 599 Tm (* Keep escalation proportionate: Match collections risk and dollar amount to mediation, counsel, or court only after the packet is complete.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 586 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 48 573 Tm (== PROCESS FLOW ==) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 560 Tm (1. Capture the trigger) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 547 Tm (Save the notice, portal message, invoice, or verbal summary that started the dispute about) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 534 Tm (exhaustion, jurisdiction, and evidence preservation. Note the date received.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 521 Tm (2. Pull controlling text) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 508 Tm (Locate the statute, CC&R, rule, and fine-schedule language that supposedly authorizes action) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 495 Tm (on exhaustion, jurisdiction, and evidence preservation.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 482 Tm (3. Build the evidence spine) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 469 Tm (Assemble dated photos, correspondence, ledgers, and comparables that speak directly to) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 456 Tm (whether court is proportionate to the dispute.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 443 Tm (4. Choose the procedural path) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 430 Tm (Pick cure, informal dispute, formal hearing, payment under protest, ADR, or counsel based on) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 417 Tm (deadlines and stakes around exhaustion, jurisdiction, and evidence preservation.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 404 Tm (5. Submit a written ask) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 391 Tm (Send one clear remedy request \(waive, reduce, re-notice, or reverse\) tied to whether court) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 378 Tm (is proportionate to the dispute, with exhibits attached.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 365 Tm (6. Confirm the outcome in writing) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 352 Tm (Demand or calendar a written decision, update your ledger notes, and decide whether) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 339 Tm (escalation is still proportionate.) Tj
